{"type": "tool_use", "timestamp": 1793896817955, "sessionID": "ses_e536b0940ffearbxkl68r5uS8a", "part": {"type": "tool", "tool": "knowledge_search_docs", "callID": "call_99da68d50b2746b9ba1f9042fd56a6d5", "state": {"status": "completed", "input": {"query": "NotificationsService stores database notifications storage", "k": 3}, "output": "[notifications-service#Data]\nNotificationsService: Data\nIt stores queued messages in the notifications Redis instance. A message stays queued until a provider accepts it or its retries run out.\n\n[notifications-service#Overview]\nNotificationsService: Overview\nNotificationsService exposes the NotificationsAPI. Any service that needs to send an email, an SMS, or a push message hands it to this API instead of talking to a provider directly.\n\n[notifications-service#Operations]\nNotificationsService: Operations\nProvider credentials rotate monthly. During a rotation the queue keeps accepting messages and holds them until the new credentials load.", "metadata": {"truncated": false}, "title": "", "time": {"start": 1793896814877, "end": 1793896817895}}, "metadata": {"openai": {"itemId": "fc_0c8de636179c418e016aecb16e165487d191b52145f43c5456"}}, "id": "prt_1ac95165e0016JqJqU7ImUB1o6", "sessionID": "ses_e536b0940ffearbxkl68r5uS8a", "messageID": "msg_1ac94fefb001rZRb45X0UXeWDX"}}
